(1) THE SAWTOOTH FLOOR  mu >= 1/49 - g^2/(4ab):
    4000 pairs (ratio <= 13): violations = 0

(2) DILATION INVARIANCE  rho(ga, gb) = rho(a, b):
    300 (a,b,g) triples: failures = 0

(3) THE PRIMITIVE THRESHOLD.  After gcd reduction the floor is
    1/49 - 1/(4a'b'), POSITIVE iff a'b' > 49/4 = 12.25, i.e. a'b' >= 13.
    So only finitely many primitive pairs need a direct check:
    primitive pairs with a'b' <= 12: 15 of them
    all have rho > 0; the minimum over them is rho(1, 12) = 1/84 = 0.011905

(4) THE COMBINED FLOOR on comparable 7-blocks (the DENSE CORE regime):
    per pair: max( 1/49 - g^2/(4ab),  the small-primitive table value )
    400 comparable 7-blocks: floor sum <= 0 in 0/400
    floor sum range [0.105661, 0.149569]   (THM-1012 gave <= 0 on ALL)

    => the SAWTOOTH floor closes the correlated regime that the
       INDEPENDENCE floor could not.  The two are exactly complementary:
       independence needs b >> a; the sawtooth needs ab large after
       gcd reduction -- which comparable blocks automatically satisfy.
